# Dark UI: Text and Hover

Hermes terminals use a dark theme. Follow this for all UI work (WPF, web, dialogs):

## Rule

**Light text → dark background.** The same pairing applies to **hover, focus, pressed, and selected** states.

Never use light/white backgrounds on hover for dark-themed controls.

## WPF

- Override the default `Button` template — the stock template adds a light hover background.
- Hover: keep background dark/transparent; change text color, border, or a slightly lighter **dark** shade (e.g. `#2B3139` → `#383f49`).
- Use shared styles such as `DarkLinkBtnStyle`, `SecondaryBtnStyle`, `LeverageChipBtnStyle`.

```xml
<!-- ✅ GOOD: hover only brightens text, background stays transparent/dark -->
<Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
    <Setter TargetName="Label" Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="#F8D12F"/>
    <Setter TargetName="Root" Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
</Trigger>

<!-- ❌ BAD: default Button hover or explicit light background -->
<Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="#F0F0F0"/>
</Trigger>
```

## Palette reference

| Role | Color |
|------|-------|
| Background | `#0B0E11`, `#181A20`, `#2B3139` |
| Hover (dark controls) | `#383f49`, `#252C3B` |
| Text | `#EAECEF` |
| Muted text | `#848E9C` |
| Accent / links | `#F0B90B` → `#F8D12F` on hover |
